# Panel 218's R2, item 3, 2026-10-17, lane land215 (found by its completeness
# critic: `R_CALL`, `{ g_divmin(), 2 }`, built and printed `-2147483648 2` at
# `-O0` and `0 2` at `-O2`, since no record accessor was asked).
#
# A record constant's accessor is asked as a scalar's is: its leaf, a call
# dividing `INT_MIN` by -1, runs under the checks and traps.
#
# Corrected 2026-10-17, the same day (panel 221's S, defect 2116): a call is
# no constant, so the record is refused `ffi_not_constant` when its unit
# compiles, before the probe runs; the probe still asks a record's accessor,
# which a constant's leaf can reach only through an operation, never a call.

extern "fixedbugs-2075-calls.h"
    record Pair tag pair
        x: i32
        y: i32
    constant C_PAIR: Pair  #~ ffi_not_constant

function main()
    v = C_PAIR
    print(v.x)
